{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7876107","formula":"C₁₃H₁₇NO₂","hill":"C13H17NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"UWA-101"},"descriptions":{"en":"UWA-101, also known as α-cyclopropyl-3,4-methylenedioxyphenethylamine (α-cPr-MDPEA), is a phenethylamine derivative researched as a potential treatment for Parkinson's disease. Its chemical structure is very similar to that of the illegal drug MDMA, the only difference being the replacement of the α-methyl group with an α-cyclopropyl group. MDMA has been found in animal studies and reported in unauthorised human self-experiments to be effective in the short-term relief of side-effects of Parkinson's disease therapy, most notably levodopa-induced dyskinesia."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":17756669,"mass":219.28,"charge":0,"smiles":"CNC(CC1=CC2=C(C=C1)OCO2)C3CC3","inchikey":"DNROCNZQNQSVOG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)-1-cyclopropyl-N-methylethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"17756669","atoms":33,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.962,"y":1.152,"z":-1.017,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.861,"y":-0.266,"z":0.712,"el":"O"},{"x":3.849,"y":-0.393,"z":-0.482,"el":"N"},{"x":2.208,"y":1.337,"z":-0.149,"el":"C"},{"x":2.797,"y":2.289,"z":0.852,"el":"C"},{"x":1.321,"y":2.014,"z":0.855,"el":"C"},{"x":2.483,"y":-0.138,"z":-0.011,"el":"C"},{"x":1.476,"y":-1.002,"z":-0.806,"el":"C"},{"x":0.056,"y":-0.833,"z":-0.377,"el":"C"},{"x":4.346,"y":-1.651,"z":0.05,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.739,"y":0.144,"z":-0.981,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.468,"y":-1.66,"z":0.632,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.045,"y":0.262,"z":-0.55,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.793,"y":-1.52,"z":1.049,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.558,"y":-0.547,"z":0.438,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.111,"y":0.811,"z":-0.214,"el":"C"},{"x":2.158,"y":1.672,"z":-1.179,"el":"H"},{